# 1. Factorial (bench/references.md §1), as the nearest Phase-1 program.
#
#   λn:Num. if n == 0 then 1 else n * ⦇⦈
#
# The recursive call `factorial(n - 1)` is an empty hole: Phase 1 has no
# recursion (it arrives in Phase 6), and a hole is exactly the honest way to
# say "an expression belongs here that cannot be written yet".

# λn:Num. ⦇⦈
construct-lam
move-parent
set-binder-id 0
set-ann Num
move-child 0

# if ⦇⦈ == ⦇⦈ then ⦇⦈ else ⦇⦈
construct-if
construct-binop eq
construct-var 0
move-next-sibling
construct-num 0

# then 1
move-parent
move-next-sibling
construct-num 1

# else n * ⦇⦈
move-next-sibling
construct-var 0
construct-binop mul
